 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "If it can happen",
     "texto": [
      "For a possible condition, it is very common to use the present in both parts: **Hvis jeg har tid, kommer jeg.** = If I have time, I'll come.",
      "You can also use **vil** or **skal** in the main clause if you want to express intention or plan. Don't use **ville** only as a future marker: it usually presents the result as hypothetical or polite."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "If it's imaginary",
     "texto": [
      "If it's a dream or something that's not going to happen, use the past tense and **ville**: **Hvis jeg havde tid, ville jeg komme.** = If I had time, I would come.",
      "Careful: **Hvis jeg vil** (if I want to) is real. **Hvis jeg ville** (if I wanted to) is imaginary."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Without «hvis»",
     "texto": [
      "You can put the verb first and drop **hvis**: **Havde jeg tid, ville jeg komme.** = If I had time, I would come.",
      "It's more formal and shows in written language."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
